From: DIR-842 R1 port
Subject: [PATCH] net: skbuff: symbolize the skb_panic caller

skb_panic() prints the return address raw, which on a stripped router image is
an unsearchable number. %pS resolves it to func+off/size [module], which is what
turned a recurring wlan1 skb_under_panic into a one-line diagnosis here.

--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ static void skb_panic(struct sk_buff *sk
 static void skb_panic(struct sk_buff *skb, unsigned int sz, void *addr,
 		      const char msg[])
 {
-	pr_emerg("%s: text:%px len:%d put:%d head:%px data:%px tail:%#lx end:%#lx dev:%s\n",
+	pr_emerg("%s: text:%pS len:%d put:%d head:%px data:%px tail:%#lx end:%#lx dev:%s\n",
 		 msg, addr, skb->len, sz, skb->head, skb->data,
 		 (unsigned long)skb->tail, (unsigned long)skb->end,
 		 skb->dev ? skb->dev->name : "<NULL>");
